ButterEye: model paths without the 256-byte stack buffers (POSIX builds).

load_param_model's #else branch - the branch Fedora builds, and every other
POSIX build with it - sprintfs its two paths into two fixed char[256] stack
buffers out of modeldir, which is the user's own model_path passed straight
through ButterEye. Measured (packaging/macos/RIFE-SPIKE.md, "The model-path
abort"): the threshold is exactly 242 characters, the first length at which
"<modeldir>/flownet.param" and its terminator no longer fit (241 + 14 + 1 =
256), and past it the plugin does not return an error - the process ABORTS.
Exit 134, SIGABRT, taking the whole vspipe or mpv with it, after parampath has
run over into modelpath (the path on stderr has lost both its head and its
tail). 242 characters is reachable in ordinary use: a deep user-chosen model
folder, a non-default package prefix, or one of the long per-user temporary
directories macOS hands out.

Build the two paths as std::string, which has no limit, and keep everything
else about the function as it was. This is the same family of bug as the
swprintf("%s") that made every Windows frame black with no error; that one is
fixed by buttereye-vs-rife-ncnn-windows-paths.patch, in the #if _WIN32 half of
the same split, which this patch does not touch.

--- a/RIFE/rife.cpp
+++ b/RIFE/rife.cpp
@@ -110,13 +110,16 @@
 #else
 static void load_param_model(ncnn::Net& net, const std::string& modeldir, const char* name)
 {
-    char parampath[256];
-    char modelpath[256];
-    sprintf(parampath, "%s/%s.param", modeldir.c_str(), name);
-    sprintf(modelpath, "%s/%s.bin", modeldir.c_str(), name);
+    // ButterEye: build the paths as strings. sprintf into two fixed char[256]
+    // stack buffers overflowed at a modeldir of 242 characters, with parampath
+    // running over into modelpath and the process aborting (SIGABRT) rather
+    // than reporting a path it could not use. modeldir is user input: it is
+    // ButterEye's model_path.
+    const std::string parampath = modeldir + "/" + name + ".param";
+    const std::string modelpath = modeldir + "/" + name + ".bin";
 
-    net.load_param(parampath);
-    net.load_model(modelpath);
+    net.load_param(parampath.c_str());
+    net.load_model(modelpath.c_str());
 }
 #endif
 
